# Feature branches only

`main` is closed on `pennmush-dotnet` and `mujs-space`. Do not commit, amend, or push to `main`.

## Starting a feature

1. A new feature starts from current `main`. Fetch and pull `main` first, then create the branch from that updated `main`.
2. Do not start a feature from another feature branch, and do not carry unrelated uncommitted work onto it.
3. Name the branch for the change, for example `feat/sensor-resolution`.

## While the pull request is open

Keep committing on that same branch until its pull request is merged or abandoned. Follow-up work for that change updates the open pull request. Start a new branch only for a different change, again from freshly pulled `main`.

## Commits, push, and the pull request

- Every commit has a message that says why the change was made. Do not make an empty commit or a commit with no message.
- Commit, push, and open the pull request when asked to publish the work. Push the feature branch with `-u`. Never push `main`.
- Open the pull request into `main`. Do not merge it.
- Whenever a pull request is created, put its full URL in the reply.

```text
# BAD
git checkout main
git commit -m "sensors"
git push origin main

# GOOD
git checkout main
git pull origin main
git checkout -b feat/sensor-resolution
git commit -m "feat(space): report contact resolution and heading"
git push -u origin HEAD
gh pr create
```
